WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome! -Yes.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.300
-Welcome back! It is always -- -Back in the house.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.100
-It is always great to see you.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.901
You look great. -Thank you.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.767
-Is this true, what I just -- My intro?

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.501
-Was that true? -50 years?

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:13.801
-Was that -- No. That can't be true. No. 50 years?

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:16.267
I was 20 -- That would make me 20-something --

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.701
When I was 23, I was pounding the pavement in New York.

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.467
-Yeah. -Trying to find a job.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.634
-Yeah, you weren't getting -- -I was going to auditions

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:26.200
and, you know, jumping the subway turnstile.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.701
-Yeah, yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.501
-Because I couldn't afford to ride -- pay for it.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:31.267
Because we weren't making any money

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.067
doing showcases or whatever, yeah.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.501
-But just this year,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.400
you're going to receive an Oscar for your work.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.701
-Yeah! -And, so, congratulations.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:39.901
-Thank you. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.501
-Come on. How great is that?

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:46.734
-You know, it's pretty dope to, like, have an Oscar presented

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.968
to you by the governors of the Motion Picture Academy.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.434
-That's exactly right.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.133
-The other way you to get it is cool, you know, be voted on

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.367
because you did a great picture,

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:57.000
but, I mean, this is like saying that, you know,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.901
I've done what I set out to do,

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:00.634
which was be a great entertainer,

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.133
get people come to the movies, have a good time.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.167
-Yeah, and you actually -- You've done more than that.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.834
-Grab some stuff, and, you know --

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.801
I put a couple asses in seats.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.167
-Yeah, you have.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:12.467
Are you going to do -- Is there a speech?

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:13.634
Are you going to be giving a speech?

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.801
-Yeah. Yeah, that one. The one I just gave.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.067
-You have to do something.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.200
-I've got to call some names, you know.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.434
-You know what? I was looking. There's a list of someone

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:28.367
who said the most swear words in movie history.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:30.200
And I was like, "Oh, yeah." -Who is it?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.000
Who won? -It's not you.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.400
It's Jonah Hill.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.234
-That's some bull [bleep]. I mean, that's --

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:38.367
♪♪

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.501
I mean -- I mean, no.

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:42.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.667
-That's better. No. -No way, man.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.234
-No way, man.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.667
-I mean, no way, man. -No way, man. Come on.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.667
-So Jonah. Then Leo. -Jonah Hill? Really?

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.300
-And then you. -And Leo?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.567
-That feels impossible to me.

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:55.968
-Jonah Hill then Leo. I don't --

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.067
I don't believe that. -Yeah.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.534
You have to catch up to Jonah -- -Somebody has miscounted.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:01.968
How many Jonah got?

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.267
-Jonah has 376, and you have 301.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.801
-Just curse words or a specific curse word?

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:10.300
-No. Oh, that's interesting.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.434
Because if it was THE curse word...

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.300
-Specific. -That one -- The one.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.968
-The one. -You're the champ.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.734
-Thank you. -Yeah, no problem.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:18.834
-Thank you very much.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.434
-Yeah, I wouldn't mess with that.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.033
Come on. That list is ridiculous.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:25.167
-Yeah. That's how I kicked off my Twitter account here.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.634
-Yeah. Remember that? -Yes!

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.067
-We started -- You sent your first tweet --

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.300
-My first tweet came from here. -Yeah.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.968
And do you remember what it was?

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:37.100
-"Can monkey fighters say 'fighter' on here?"

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.334
-Yeah, thank you. Thank you for editing yourself.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.868
Thank you for editing yourself.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.367
-"Can my friends say 'friend' on here?"

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.033
-Yeah, exactly. -Yeah, that.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.400
-You did that here, but then --

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.133
Now I follow you on all the socials.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.167
You're a great follow on Instagram, by the way.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.167
I've been seeing a lot of your shirts.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.200
-Ah.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.601
-You have T-shirts that you wear.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.734
Just let me show you, because it's super funny.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.868
This is you.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.234
This is you with your -- with Jules.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.834
You're wearing a shirt with you as Jules

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:03.934
from "Pulp Fiction" right there.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.968
-With a pin. With a pin of me as Jules.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.067
-Wow.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.567
-So, then, I like that.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:14.367
But then here's your Nick Fury shirt.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:16.968
-One of them. Yep, yep. -That's good.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:19.734
-I got a gang of those. -Yeah, I like that one.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:24.067
Then this one is -- this is your "Shaft" shirt.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.334
-Oh, yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:26.934
-You've got, like, kind of a meaner face.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.634
-I sometimes try and match the faces on the shirts.

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:31.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. That's, like, a meaner face.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.767
-See what I can do, yeah.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.767
-And then this is my favorite one.

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:39.267
This is you wearing you wearing the "Shaft" shirt.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.033
Very meta. -Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.200
-And that's brilliant. That blew my mind.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.567
-With my -- my eye depuffer for the morning.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.901
-Is that -- -Yeah, that's what the --

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:51.100
Yeah, the little gold eye things in the morning.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.067
You have to work for some glamour.

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.467
-Yeah, come on. To look this good?

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.400
Come on, bud. Yeah.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.334
You know, you've been around for a while,

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.734
and there's a lot of kind of Internet rumors about you.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.334
And I thought maybe we could squash

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:05.634
some of those rumors tonight if you don't mind, yeah.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.434
Yeah, I'd like to maybe go through some myths

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.200
about you and you tell me if they're true or not true.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.033
-I try not to read those. -All right, ready?

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.434
-Uh-huh, yeah. -Nothing's bad.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:18.133
You once beat Tiger Woods in golf.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:20.133
That can't be true. -Complete accident.

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.467
-What?!

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:26.133
-Well, the first time I ever played St Andrews,

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.534
they paired me with him

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:31.834
in what was the Dunhill Golf Tournament, and I was a 16.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:35.133
So, they gave me my 16 shots, and I shot 78,

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.734
because he said, "Follow me."

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:39.834
And I stayed as close to him as I could and I shot 78.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.033
-Wow!

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:43.234
-Which means I beat him by about 8 strokes.

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:44.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.667
-I mean, come on. Not too shabby.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.868
That's pretty cool. That's not that bad.

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.501
Uh...

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:55.367
Two, is it true that you own over 800 Kangol hats?

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:58.167
-My wife got rid of about 500 of them.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:01.601
-Okay. So you're down to 300. -I'm down to 300.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.467
-When did you start wearing those?

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:06.501
-Oh, geez, when I stole my first one

00:05:06.501 --> 00:05:08.400
out of my grandfather's closet.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.968
-Yeah. Exactly right. -Long, long time ago.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.467
-Do you remember what color? Black?

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:13.934
-My grandfather's? -Yeah.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.367
-No, it was like a --

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.667
It was a plaidy hat, you know? It's one of those patterns.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.734
-Stylish, too, yeah. -Yeah.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.834
-Number three, Samuel L. Jackson does not do

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.133
more than three takes of any scene in a movie.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.601
Is that true?

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.267
-If I can help it. -Really?

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.467
-Well, I have to have a really good explanation

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:31.267
when you need more than three.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.367
-Yeah, that's true. -Somebody's messing up.

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.000
Because it ain't me.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:41.734
It's like -- Is the focus puller --

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:43.834
"Is there anything I can do to make this better?

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.000
Can I help?" You know?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.801
Or, "Do we need to hire somebody else?"

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:47.934
You know. -Yeah.

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.934
Did you ever have, like, a director that's going,

00:05:49.934 --> 00:05:52.000
"Let's just do one for fun"?

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.100
-Yeah, I have them say that. -Yeah.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.567
-And you don't do that? -No.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:59.300
-No. I mean, because that's, like, crazy.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.734
Because I don't get to go to the editing room.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.100
And if they want to try something different,

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:07.000
that means they're going to look at that first,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.868
because that's who they are.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.300
And it's like -- I don't know. They don't get that option.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.267
-I love you. That's just so good.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:15.467
Oh, this one.

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:17.234
You had the "Star Wars" prop team

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:20.234
engrave your lightsaber with a special acronym.

00:06:20.234 --> 00:06:21.400
Is that true?

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.868
-No, they did that because they loved me.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:25.801
I didn't ask for it.

00:06:25.801 --> 00:06:27.834
-They did that because they -- -When they gave it to me,

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:30.767
When the shoot was over, when they presented it to me,

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:33.534
it had "BMF" on the on/off button.

00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:36.434
-Yeah, and what does "BMF" stand for?

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:37.801
-Bad, my friend.

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.868 --> 00:06:43.334
-That's exactly right.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:46.400
You're cool enough to actually take a photograph of this

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.234
so we can show it to everyone right here.

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:49.667
This is actually real.

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.334
I did not -- We've never seen this engravement.

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:52.434
Look right there.

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:54.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:55.968
That's what I'm talking about!

00:06:55.968 --> 00:06:58.567
That's love for Samuel L. Jackson right there.

00:06:58.567 --> 00:07:00.100
-Yes, it was. Yes, it was.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.934
-Yeah, more with Samuel L. Jackson after the break.

00:07:01.934 --> 00:07:03.701
We're gonna talk about his new Apple TV+ series.

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:04.968
Stick around.

